Appendix E: Pre-Registration Checklist and Hyperparameters

This appendix provides additional details for the experimental protocol, including pre-registration items and recommended hyperparameter ranges.

E.1 Pre-Registration Checklist

Prior to conducting any empirical evaluation, the following items must be registered:

· Exact definition of technology entities and data sources.
· Preprocessing steps for text extraction and performance metric parsing.
· Graph construction method and edge weight formula.
· Latent dimension $d$ and number of sufficient statistics $k$.
· Encoder, decoder, and prior network architectures (layers, units, activations).
· Optimization hyperparameters (learning rate, batch size, epochs, early stopping criteria).
· Event thresholds $Q^*$ for each forecast target.
· Evaluation metrics and statistical testing procedures.
· Baseline model specifications (including LLM prompt templates).
· Data leakage prevention mechanisms (real-time entity resolution, timestamp filtering).

E.2 Recommended Hyperparameter Ranges

· Embedding model: SciBERT or SPECTER with output dimension 768.
· UMAP: n_neighbors = 15, min_dist = 0.1, n_components = 50.
· HDBSCAN: min_cluster_size = 10, metric = 'euclidean'.
· Latent dimension: $d \in \{8, 16, 32\}$ (selected via validation).
· Sufficient statistics: $k = 2$ (e.g., $T(z) = (z, z^2)$).
· Encoder network: LSTM or Transformer with 128 hidden units, 2 layers.
· Decoder network: MLP with 256 hidden units, 2 layers.
· Prior transition network: MLP with 128 hidden units, 2 layers.
· Optimizer: Adam with learning rate $\eta = 1 \times 10^{-3}$.
· Batch size: $B = 64$.
· Epochs: maximum 200 with early stopping patience 20.
· Bootstrap samples: $B_s = 1000$.

These values are starting points; final choices should be justified via cross-validation on training periods only.

