Description:
The encoder takes the entire history up to time $t$ and outputs parameters of a Gaussian approximate posterior. A latent sample is drawn via reparameterization. The decoder computes the likelihood of observations, while the prior (conditioned on past state, graph neighbors, and covariates) provides a regularizer. The ELBO combines both terms, and gradients are backpropagated to update all networks.

